<title>UK: GOLF-FIVE EXEMPT FROM OPEN QUALIFYING.</title>
<headline>GOLF-FIVE EXEMPT FROM OPEN QUALIFYING.</headline>
<dateline>TROON, Scotland 1997-07-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Five players were made exempt from final qualifying for next week's British Open after the Loch Lomond World Invitational on Saturday.</p>
<p>They were Retief Goosen of South Africa, third after a course record 62, Ignacio Garrido of Spain and Ross McFarlane, Jamie Spence and Russell Claydon of Britain.</p>
